{% doc %}
  Restores readable text on routes that emit NO colour-scheme class.

  layout/theme.liquid:67-71 puts the FIRST colour scheme on :root, and scheme-1
  in config/settings_data.json has text #000000, so :root carries
  --color-foreground: 0,0,0. theme.liquid:108 then paints
  body { color: rgba(var(--color-foreground), 0.75) }.

  sections/main-404.liquid, main-login.liquid and main-account.liquid emit ZERO
  `color-` classes (grep -c returns 0 for all three), so against the forced
  html,body{background:#000!important} at theme.liquid:275 they render BLACK ON
  BLACK — functionally blank. The empty cart's LOG IN link
  (sections/main-cart-items.liquid:366) leads straight into one.

  Fixed by overriding the TOKEN, not a colour, so every descendant that reads
  --color-foreground inherits correctly. scheme-4 is the theme's own
  white-on-black scheme (text #ffffff / background #000000).

  @param {string} [drop_url] - Where the "Back to the drop" link points.
                               Defaults to /collections/supreme-leader.
  @example
    {% render 'ak-drop-safety', drop_url: '/collections/supreme-leader' %}
{% enddoc %}

{%- style -%}
  html.ak-drop-safe,
  html.ak-drop-safe body{
    --color-foreground: 255,255,255;
  }
  html.ak-drop-safe body{
    color: rgba(255,255,255,.86);
  }
  html.ak-drop-safe #MainContent,
  html.ak-drop-safe #MainContent .gradient{
    background: transparent !important;
    background-image: none !important;
  }
  html.ak-drop-safe h1,
  html.ak-drop-safe h2,
  html.ak-drop-safe h3,
  html.ak-drop-safe .title,
  html.ak-drop-safe legend,
  html.ak-drop-safe label{
    color:#fff;
  }
  html.ak-drop-safe a{ color:#ff33ff; }
  html.ak-drop-safe a:hover{ color:#fff; }

  /* the 404 CTA takes background #121212 / text #fff from :root's scheme-1,
     which is near-invisible on the forced #000 ground */
  html.ak-drop-safe .button,
  html.ak-drop-safe a.button{
    background:#fff;color:#000;border:2px solid #fff;
  }
  html.ak-drop-safe .button:hover,
  html.ak-drop-safe a.button:hover{
    background:#ff33ff;border-color:#ff33ff;color:#12000f;
  }

  html.ak-drop-safe input,
  html.ak-drop-safe textarea,
  html.ak-drop-safe select{
    background:#0d0d0d;color:#fff;border:1px solid rgba(255,255,255,.3);
  }
{%- endstyle -%}

{%- comment -%}
  These eight routes contain ZERO links back into the drop journey. The 404's own
  CTA points at the old site, so it is replaced rather than restyled. The .button
  rule is deliberately gated on template.name — unscoped, it would hide the login,
  register and save buttons on the seven customers/* templates this also renders on.
{%- endcomment -%}
{%- if template.name == '404' -%}
  {%- style -%}
    html.ak-drop-safe .template-404 a.button,
    html.ak-drop-safe main a.button{ display:none !important; }
  {%- endstyle -%}
{%- endif -%}

<a class="akds-back" href="{{ drop_url | default: '/collections/supreme-leader' }}">&larr; Back to the drop</a>

{%- style -%}
  html.ak-drop-safe .akds-back{
    display:inline-block;margin:1.6rem auto;
    font-size:15px;font-weight:600;letter-spacing:.11em;text-transform:uppercase;
    color:#fff;text-decoration:none;
    border-bottom:2px solid #e31300;padding-bottom:3px;
  }
  html.ak-drop-safe .akds-back:hover{ color:#e31300; }
{%- endstyle -%}

<script>document.documentElement.classList.add('ak-drop-safe');</script>
